#14: choose action by ratio of forces — small number of high-value lessons vs. many: with many lessons (56), don't load all; narrow.

#11: foreknowledge from people, pay for it — knowledge of what fails comes from the agents' own reports (the six whys) not from introspection; the store must be fed by the failure records, and the maintenance has a cost.

