**How one-type vs all-agents lessons are kept apart:**
- `scope:` field, not folders. Reason: folders duplicate the delivery logic and a lesson that applies to one engine is still worth the main agent knowing (it should not brief that engine with a task it can't do). But scope decides *who it is pushed to*, not who may read it. Keep one directory, one file per lesson, `scope: all | engine:claude | engine:opencode | ...`. If scopes multiply (e.g., tool-specific quirks), a `scope: [engine:opencode, engine:agy]` list. One index generated from front-matter.

