**Costs and risks:**
- Partial coverage: the guard sees Bash writes only as a command line (fact) → lessons keyed to shell edits (`sed -i`, heredoc, `python - <<`) will miss. So the hook is a net, not a wall. (#2: you cannot make the enemy certain — the repeat cannot be made impossible, only made unlikely; my #2)
- Noise: a lesson on every write is a tax on every write; over-matching globs is the likely failure. Cap + trigger precision. (#8: speed/value — the brief wants less noise; #15: 爱民可烦 — a store that wants to save every mistake becomes a nuisance.)
- Store rot: 56 sections and growing; without retirement it becomes unread. Retire a lesson when a check enforces it; keep a pointer. (#15 必生 — the one set on living = keeping every insight alive; #3 whole vs broken: one canonical copy, not copies per engine)
- Divergence: agent lesson + project fact can disagree; the project fact must not be duplicated in the store. (#3)
